<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SAfrica April prov financing figures 4.65 bln rand.</title>
<headline>SAfrica April prov financing figures 4.65 bln rand.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financing of 2,683.9 million rand was obtained in government bonds while net short-term loans increased by 518.4 million rand during April this year, the South African Finance Department said on Monday.</p>
<p>In addition, 1,450.0 million rand was transferred from the Strategic Fuel Fund (SFF) in respect of proceeds generated by the commercial activities of the SFF Association and through the sale of strategic crude oil stock and interest received.</p>
<p>Total financing for April amounted to 4,652.3 million rand, the department said in a statement.</p>
<p>			     April 1997		 Budget</p>
<p>							    1997/98</p>
<p>			     (R'million)</p>
<p>Government bonds	 2,683.9		    27,702.0</p>
